  "result": "The 3-field form won clearly, and it's now shipped to 100% in Development. The flag `signup_form` is archived.\n\n- **Result:** the 3-field form converted at 33.1% against 19.1% for the 6-field control (about 1,000 simulated users). Lift was +73.7%, 95% CI [35.1, 112.3]%, and win probability 100%. The results script's verdict was `ship:short_form`. That read was still labelled `final=false`, so it was the interim, not the frozen one.\n- **Code:** the work is on branch `ship-short-signup-form`, in two commits. `server.js` now serves only the 3-field form (email, password, first name). The flag check, the 6-field path and the Flagsmith SDK and tracking are removed. The SDK is gone from `package.json`, and the lockfile I'd generated for it is deleted. There's no PR because there's no remote.\n- **Rollback:** `bash scripts/rollback.sh signup_form .flagsmith-skill/rollback/signup_form-20261128T004844Z.state`. This restores the flag state, but the code on the branch no longer reads the flag.\n- **Audit log:** `.flagsmith-skill/audit.log`.\n- **Not checked:** I never started the server or loaded the page after the cleanup. I only ran `node --check` on `server.js`, which passed.",
